    "provenance": "# envelope.fill\n\nFile: `envelope.fill.svg`.\n\nAuthorship: produced 2026-10-10 by a Claude agent (Opus 5.5) for Satin, clean-room. Derived from Framework7 Icons 5.0.5 (MIT) outline geometry: 56-unit viewBox, ~3.8-unit regular stroke, round caps and joins, one nonzero filled path via skia-pathops.\n\nDescription: Fill that shares its outline's silhouette: the Framework7 outline's outer silhouette made solid, with its interior detail strokes knocked out. Slash and badge variants are the base fill with a gap cut around a slash or badge fitted to the Framework7 outline; open-box variants are a solid box with the tool cut through. Replaces Framework7's separately drawn fill, which had a different shape.\n\nConstruction update (2026-10-10): the outline's silhouette made solid, with round-ended 2.6-unit seams on the Framework7 stroke centres. The flap V is filleted through the outline's own rounded bottom. Each lower fold ends in a clean T on the flap, and every seam stops one wall short of the edge.\n\nProvenance: no SF Symbols file, font, image, screenshot or exported path was opened, traced or recalled. Only Framework7 Icons SVGs were used, as geometry sources or style references.",
